      "description": "Each container and each systemd service as one, with all the processes it runs, stacked. On the Proxmox host each VM is one. Docker's own services are one, and Ubuntu's own are one. Counted is what an application needs to keep running, as Kubernetes measures it (the working set): its own data, memory it shares, kernel memory used for it, and the files it is using. Files it read and no longer uses are not counted. The Max column is what to size the machine for. Everything else is the kernel and processes outside the applications listed.",
